WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.423
- [Mark] All right.

00:00:02.423 --> 00:00:04.480
So Michael, Michael Franzese.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.130
- That's it, you got it.
- Excellent.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.410
Let me do a brief intro

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.580
and you'll maybe help me
with some of the details.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.080
So the best story that
sums up everything is,

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.970
back in the '80s "Fortune
Magazine" did a cover story

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.820
on the 50 biggest, most
money-making mob bosses.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:23.653
- Right.

00:00:23.653 --> 00:00:25.530
- [Mark] And you were, I
think, number 18 at the time?

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:26.420
- Correct.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.880
- [Mark] And your father
was also a mobster?

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:31.713
- He was.

00:00:31.713 --> 00:00:35.663
- [Mark] And you had an
illustrious career in the mob.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.700
I guess, where should we start
with your childhood, I guess?

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.230
- Yeah, I guess, you know, I mean,

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.520
obviously I grew up under that influence.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.650
My dad was a very prominent figure

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:49.747
during the 1960s especially,

00:00:49.747 --> 00:00:51.160
he's, kind of, like the
John Gotti of his day.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.120
- Oh, is that right?
- Yeah.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.480
He was a tremendous amount
of publicity, you know,

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.000
a lot of media attention,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.540
a major, major target of law enforcement.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.437
It was almost like, you
know, I used to think

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:04.060
"Why did they pick him
out out of all the people

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.810
"that were around at that point in time?"

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:08.460
But he really was the kind of media star

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.633
at that point in time.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.420
- [Mark] Apparently there's stories of him

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.690
and Marilyn Monroe
running around together?

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.550
- Yeah, well, you know,
he revealed that to me

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.780
a little bit later on after
my mother passed away.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.957
'Cause I asked him, I said,
"Dad, you know, why you?

00:01:20.957 --> 00:01:24.097
"Why did they, you know, have
this concentration fascination

00:01:24.097 --> 00:01:25.630
"with you at the time?"

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:29.670
Long story short, he said
he was dating Marilyn Monroe

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.360
and Bobby Kennedy found out about it,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.480
and from that point on
Kennedy made my father

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.140
his target and ordered
Hoover to go after him.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.980
And you know, it makes
sense, I'll be honest.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.110
My dad, sometimes, you
know, he embellishes things

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:44.030
a little bit, but that story makes sense.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:45.880
- [Mark] And he knows how to
keep a secret very well too.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.713
- He does, yes.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.540
- [Mark] So as a kid growing
up with a father like your dad,

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.603
how was your childhood
different than most people?

00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:59.450
- Was a lot different,

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.740
I mean, you know, back then
the law enforcement tactics

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.080
against organized crime were
very different than today.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.170
I mean, today everything's very covert,

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:10.000
undercover informants,
high-tech surveillance.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.860
Back then when a guy
was under investigation

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:12.947
they wanted you to know about it.

00:02:12.947 --> 00:02:14.890
And my dad was under investigation

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.510
maybe seven or eight
different agencies, FBI, IRS,

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.430
Queen Detective, Brooklyn
DA, they were all there.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.570
And they would have a car
parked around my house

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.400
24 hours a day, seven days a week

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.150
'cause he was under constant surveillance.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.370
So, you know, I was one of seven kids,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.820
and every time we went anywhere

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.180
we had a parade of law
enforcement vehicles following us.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.670
It was just the way it was.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.140
And that was for several years.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.820
And so, you know, I mean,
look, my dad was my hero,

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.470
he was a great father, I loved him.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:44.870
So I grew up actually
hating law enforcement,

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.840
and I had many little scuffles
with them as a kid, you know,

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.493
and so that was kind of
the environment I was in.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.960
- [Mark] And then your
plans, as you grew up

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.360
were not to follow in
your dad's footsteps.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.419
You were actually pre pre-med, I think?

00:03:00.419 --> 00:03:01.320
- Yeah, I was a pre-med student.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.280
I was an athlete.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.870
I had no desire to be,
become a member of his life,

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.270
mainly because my dad
didn't discuss it with me.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.510
He didn't talk to me about it.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:10.623
He'd encourage me.

00:03:11.522 --> 00:03:12.650
You know, one thing I really respected

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.780
about him, many thing's
obviously, but he never

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.990
brought what was going
on in the outside world

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:17.950
into our house.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.110
In the house we were a family.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.850
So he never talked about it.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:23.530
He didn't acknowledge who he
was, you know, none of that.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.730
So to me, I'm playing ball,

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.390
you know, if you said to me as a kid,

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.750
who would I like to emulate?

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.150
What would I like to be?

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.460
I wanted to play center field
for the New York Yankees,

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.143
Mickey Mantle was kinda my guy.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.640
So no, I didn't aspire to be in that life

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.320
but I was gonna be a doctor.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.200
My dad wanted me to go to medical school,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.320
so that's what I was pursuing.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.270
And, you know, until
he got in some trouble

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.853
and things changed for me.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.660
- What changed your direction?

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.610
- Well, my dad was indicted several times

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:55.760
in the early '60s, three serious charges

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.870
in the state of New York,

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.430
and he went to trial,
beat them all, you know.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.430
But then he was indicted in
federal court for masterminding

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.010
a nationwide string of
bank robberies, convicted,

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.420
sentenced to 50 years in prison.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.070
- 50?
- 50.

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.640
Which was kind of a death
sentence for him at that point,

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.110
he was 50 years old when he went in.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.470
So I figured he'd never
come out of prison alive.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:18.440
So, you know, at that time,
Joe Colombo, he kind of took me

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.273
under his wing.

00:04:19.273 --> 00:04:20.106
He had just started

00:04:20.106 --> 00:04:22.565
the Italian American Civil Rights League.

00:04:22.565 --> 00:04:23.955
- Joe Colombo is the head of the

00:04:23.955 --> 00:04:24.788
Colombo family.
- Joe Colombo

00:04:24.788 --> 00:04:26.443
was the boss of all family, yeah.

00:04:26.443 --> 00:04:27.276
- One of the Big Five Families

00:04:27.276 --> 00:04:28.200
in New York?
- Correct.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.320
And we were close, you know,

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.880
he kinda took me under his wing.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.500
My dad and him obviously were close,

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.650
my dad was his underboss.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:38.560
So, you know, I got highly
influenced by a lot of my dad's

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.670
friends saying, "Mike, what
are you doing going to school?"

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.830
If you don't help your dad
out, he's gonna die in prison.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.640
So, you know, I lost interest in school.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.100
Then I was picketing the FBI every day

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.520
with Colombo in that league.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.030
So I was meeting a lot of guys,

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.210
I was getting, you know, all the courage

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.610
that maybe the league would help my dad.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.187
So it was kind of a
direction change for me.

00:04:56.187 --> 00:04:59.010
And I went to see him
Leavenworth, and we sat down,

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.427
I said, "Dad, I'm not going to school.

00:05:00.427 --> 00:05:02.930
"If I don't help you out,
you're gonna die in here."

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.100
And, you know, we kinda
went back and forth

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.760
'cause he didn't want that for me.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.080
But he knew my mind was made up,

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:09.630
I was pretty headstrong as a kid.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:12.007
And he said, "Okay, but if
you're gonna be on the street

00:05:12.007 --> 00:05:13.830
"I want you to on the
street the right way."

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.690
And in his mind the
right way was to become

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:16.620
a member of his life.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.160
So it was at that point

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:21.093
that he proposed me from
membership into that life.

00:05:24.178 --> 00:05:26.197
- And so what's the first step?

00:05:26.197 --> 00:05:28.560
You started doing small?

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.557
- Yeah, well he sends
word downtown, you know,

00:05:30.557 --> 00:05:32.550
and he said to me, "Just
do whatever he told."

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:33.500
He knew I had it in me,

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.500
so otherwise he wouldn't have done that,

00:05:36.431 --> 00:05:38.082
and so I went,

00:05:38.082 --> 00:05:39.610
About two weeks after that visit a captain

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.240
in the family took me to see the boss.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.710
Now, many people don't
know is some people do

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.810
that Joe Colombo was assassinated

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.740
and there was an attempt on his life.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.760
He eventually died from the wounds.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.087
A new boss took over,
his name was Tom DiBella,

00:05:53.087 --> 00:05:55.470
has passed on now, and I sat with him.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.387
And he said, "I got a
message from your father,

00:05:57.387 --> 00:05:59.157
"he said, you want to
become a member of our life,

00:05:59.157 --> 00:05:59.990
"is that true?

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:00.823
I said, "Yes."

00:06:00.823 --> 00:06:01.837
He said, "Well, here's the deal,

00:06:01.837 --> 00:06:05.037
"from now on 24 hours a
day, seven days a week

00:06:05.037 --> 00:06:08.260
"you're on call to serve this
family, the Colombo family."

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.000
And to show me how serious that was,

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.787
he said, "That means
if your mother is sick

00:06:11.787 --> 00:06:13.667
"and dying and you're at her bedside,

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:14.787
"we call you to service,

00:06:14.787 --> 00:06:16.937
"you leave your mother,
you come and serve us.

00:06:16.937 --> 00:06:18.577
"From now on we're number one in your life

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:20.237
"before anything and everything.

00:06:20.237 --> 00:06:22.327
"When, if we feel you
deserve this privilege,

00:06:22.327 --> 00:06:24.240
"this honor to become a
member we'll let you know."

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.590
So I was 21, close to 22 years old,

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.690
I was in like a recruit
period where I had to do

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.220
anything and everything I was told to do

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:33.463
to prove myself worthy.

00:06:34.786 --> 00:06:36.890
- [Mark] And those included
what kind of things?

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.120
- Well, listen, you
know, it could have been

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.280
something very menial.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:40.920
There's a lot of discipline in that life,

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.190
a lot of authority, you know.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:44.870
You had a meeting at seven o'clock,

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:46.765
you weren't there at 06:30 you were late,

00:06:46.765 --> 00:06:48.590
you could never be late in that life.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:50.760
Drive the boss to a meeting,
you know, sit in a car

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:51.650
for five hours.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:54.160
God forbid you leave, you go
get a newspaper, a restroom,

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:55.960
he comes out, you're not
there, you're in trouble.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:58.410
I know I did that once paid the price.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.880
But you know, a lot of stuff like that.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:01.870
I mean, you had to show that
you could take authority

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:05.030
and that you would disciplined
and so on and forth.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.220
And then, you know, look,

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:08.610
I'm always as honest
as I can be about that.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.850
You know, the life is very violent,

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.990
and if you're part of that life,
you're part of the violence

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.320
and there's no escape.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.500
Anybody tells you differently,

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:16.920
they're either not being honest with you

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.070
or they weren't a made
member of that life.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.520
- [Mark] That went on for how many years?

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.540
- About two years, 18 months, two years,

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.710
something like that, I was
in this recruit period.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.320
- [Mark] And you were
great, everybody thought

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.577
you were a good fit?

00:07:29.577 --> 00:07:30.410
And what happened?

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.297
- It seems that way, yeah.

00:07:32.297 --> 00:07:34.820
It was Halloween night,
1975 when I was called

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:38.910
into a room with five other
gentlemen, all recruits.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.980
The interesting thing
at that point was that

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:45.130
they had an expression
just before that period

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.070
where the books were closed in that life,

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.230
meaning they weren't bringing
in any new members formally.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:53.830
And in the early '70s
they opened up the books

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:58.830
and I was inducted with guys
that were waiting 20, 25 years,

00:07:59.161 --> 00:08:00.810
they were recruits that long, yeah.

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:03.060
So it was kind of a mix
in there that night,

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.160
but we all took an oath that night,

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.990
became sworn, made members
of the Colombo family.

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:09.060
- [Mark] How many?

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:09.893
- There were six of us.

00:08:09.893 --> 00:08:10.927
- Six of you?.
- Yeah.

00:08:10.927 --> 00:08:12.580
- [Mark] And you were how old?

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.633
- I was 24.
- 24.

00:08:17.524 --> 00:08:20.500
- [Mark] So, you know, I heard a story

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.623
of those six gentlemen that
were inducted that night.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:27.870
How many of them are still around?

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:31.120
- Well, out of the six of
us, I'm the only one alive.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.340
The other five were all, they all died.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.330
And from what I understand,
they were all murdered.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.620
- [Mark] It's so dangerous
treacherous career.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.720
- It's a tough life, no doubt.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.730
- [Mark] And there was a
ceremony involved as well, right?

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:43.975
Tell me about that briefly.

00:08:43.975 --> 00:08:45.150
- It was a very solemn ceremony,

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:46.870
you know, dimly lit room, late at night,

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:48.560
they wanted you to
understand the, you know,

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.753
the seriousness of what you
were getting involved in.

00:08:51.753 --> 00:08:53.130
And we walked into a room individually,

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.500
the boss was seated at the head of

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:57.231
like a horseshoe configuration; underboss,

00:08:57.231 --> 00:08:59.400
consiglieres left and
right, and all the captains

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.233
alongside of them.

00:09:00.233 --> 00:09:02.950
We had about 15 in our
family at that point.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.610
Walked down the aisle,
stood in front of the boss

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:05.570
held out my hand.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:07.410
He takes a knife, cuts my fingers,

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.630
some blood drops on the floor.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:09.783
This is a blood oath.

00:09:10.956 --> 00:09:12.510
I cupped my hands, he
took a picture of a saint,

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:15.440
Catholic altar card, put it
in my hands, lit a flame.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.960
Didn't hurt, it burned quickly,
it was merely symbolic.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:19.557
And he said, "Tonight, Michael Franzese

00:09:19.557 --> 00:09:22.880
"you are born again into a new
life, into La Cosa Nostra,"

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.207
this thing of ours.

00:09:24.207 --> 00:09:25.787
"Violate what you know about this life,

00:09:25.787 --> 00:09:28.367
"betray your brothers and
you will die and burn in hell

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.180
"like the Saint is burning in your hands."

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.407
And he said, "Do you accept?"

00:09:31.407 --> 00:09:32.240
"Yes, I do."

00:09:36.285 --> 00:09:39.033
- And then what changes
after that happens?

00:09:39.033 --> 00:09:40.070
You can start becoming who?

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:42.980
- Well, you know, you
kind of find your way

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:46.910
in that life and you
either, how can I put it?

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:49.890
You separate yourself
in being in one category

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.760
or the other, even
though we're all capable

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.470
of doing what we need to do
and what we're told to do,

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:56.610
but some of us were
earners, I would call us,

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.440
and some of us weren't, you know.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.820
And unfortunately the
greater percentage of us

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:03.390
were not earners.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:05.290
But in our family at that time, you know,

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.410
we had 115 made guys, guys
that actually took the oath,

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:09.430
a lot of more are associates,

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.360
but guys that actually took the oath.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.576
Out of the 115, I think 20
of us were real earners.

00:10:14.576 --> 00:10:15.620
- [Mark] Some were the brains
and some were the brawn.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:16.680
- Yeah, yeah.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.900
And you know, the other
95 guys they're, you know,

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:21.372
getting by doing some of
the heavy work, you know.

00:10:21.372 --> 00:10:24.180
Who's got a gambling issue,
who's getting a union job

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:27.653
you know, we tried to take
care of them, but you know,

00:10:28.748 --> 00:10:29.581
it's just the way it goes.

00:10:29.581 --> 00:10:30.414
Like anything else

00:10:30.414 --> 00:10:32.770
you kind of separate
yourself in that life.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.883
- [Mark] And what kind of, I
mean, so what were the first

00:10:34.883 --> 00:10:38.766
like business endeavors
that you were engaged in?

00:10:38.766 --> 00:10:40.870
- Well, you know, I was
fortunate in that I understood

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:44.320
early on how to use that life
to benefit me in business,

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:45.910
and I had a head for business I would say.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.970
I was very aggressive on the street,

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.560
brought some new things into the family.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:52.830
But I really started out, you
know, my dad had me working

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.910
in an autobody shop when
he was home, you know,

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:56.560
just helping some guys,

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:59.640
so I started out in the car business,

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:02.130
that turned into me owning two dealerships

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.470
at that time, I built it up.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.320
I had a used car lot, I
had a leasing company,

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:06.153
I had body shop.

00:11:06.153 --> 00:11:09.580
So I had a pretty big
business that I, kind of, grew

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.570
in a short period of time.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:14.270
And then, you know, along with that life

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.580
you saw people come your way and they

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:19.140
they offer you deals, and, you know,

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:20.400
you accept or you reject

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.700
depending upon the quality
of what's going on.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:24.743
And before you know it

00:11:24.743 --> 00:11:25.810
I had several different interests.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.720
I owned nightclubs, I had restaurants,

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.910
I had, again, a leasing company.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.583
I ended up with a production
company in California.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:37.027
So I had a bunch of
different things going on

00:11:37.027 --> 00:11:39.813
and was able to turn things
into successful operations.

00:11:39.813 --> 00:11:40.984
- [Mark] That's great.

00:11:40.984 --> 00:11:44.580
And then eventually you got
you hooked into something

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:48.070
that was what, I guess, has been described

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:49.310
as the most lucrative thing the mob

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:52.550
has ever been involved
in since Al Capone, yeah?

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.630
- Yeah, it actually the gas business.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:58.610
And, you know, very long
story short, I got approached

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:03.350
by someone at a small
wholesale operation selling gas

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:05.080
out in Long Island.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.410
And there was two guys from another family

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.230
trying to extort him, shake him down,

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:10.360
and he came to me to help.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:12.610
I was kind of the guy on Long Island.

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:15.660
And so I helped him out and together

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.700
we devise a scheme to
defraud the government

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.170
out of tax on every gallon of gasoline.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:25.170
And that grew from a very small
operation to at its height,

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:28.200
after eight years, I ran
it for about eight years.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:32.270
We had over 350 stations that
we either owned or operated.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.500
We had 18 wholesale
companies that were licensed

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.970
to collect the tax on
every gallon of gasoline.

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:41.500
And we built that up to
selling half a billion gallons

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:43.830
of gas a month, and we
were taking down 20, 30

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.820
40 cents a gallon,
depending upon the deals.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.820
So, you know, it was very lucrative,

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:50.317
we brought in, you know,
at times seven, eight

00:12:50.317 --> 00:12:51.210
$10 million a week.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:52.957
- A week?
- It was that big, yeah.

00:12:52.957 --> 00:12:54.380
It was a big operation.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:56.820
I brought the Russians
in from a Brighton Beach,

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.670
and it was a, you know, it was described

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.180
as the most lucrative operation

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:02.640
since the days of prohibition,

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.180
and I saw it that way also.

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:07.890
- [Mark] And that made you
star amongst your cohorts?

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.140
- When you're making that kind of money,

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.590
money is power in that life,

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:12.300
and, you know, I got the attention

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:13.550
of some of the other families.

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:17.170
And so I made, you know,
relationships, which is important

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:19.440
in that life to have allies
in the other families.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.530
So tried to spread some of the
wealth around and, you know,

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.640
make people happy, and money
buys loyalty in that regard,

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:28.520
so yeah, I started to
make a name for myself.

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:29.360
- [Mark] That's great.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:31.650
At one of the funniest little stories

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:33.000
I heard you share once was,

00:13:36.469 --> 00:13:39.330
is it "Big Vinnie" that that
helped get this off the ground,

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:41.551
and he came in with a box one day?

00:13:41.551 --> 00:13:42.790
He was a butcher.
- Yeah, Vinnie,

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.760
Vinnie was a butcher and
he was one of my guys,

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:48.160
trusted guy, big, you
know, ominous looking guy,

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.000
big scar across the top
of his head, a butcher.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.090
And so I had put him with this guy, Larry

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.760
that came to me with this
whole proposal for gas.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:58.390
And after two weeks in
the operation, he comes

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:01.240
to my house with, he used to
bring me meet every Saturday

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.700
and now he's carrying a big box,

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:04.997
and I said, "What do we having a party?

00:14:04.997 --> 00:14:06.630
"What are we gonna do with all this meat?"

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.530
Brings it in the kitchen,
puts it on the table,

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:09.900
and he says, "It ain't me boss."

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.620
He said, "It's the first
week's taking at gas station."

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:16.500
Opens it up $320,000,
smelled like gasoline,

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.560
smelled up the whole kitchen,

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.875
but I didn't care at that point.

00:14:19.875 --> 00:14:22.160
But we grew that 320 and too, like I said,

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.880
close to $10 million a week.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:26.870
- Wow! And so at some point

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:31.870
I'm sure, the Colombo
boss at the time was--

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:32.703
- Persico.
- Persico.

00:14:32.703 --> 00:14:33.773
- Carmine Persico, yeah.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:38.270
- [Mark] What was his reaction to this?

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.450
- Well, you know, when I
knew what I had, you know,

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:42.790
you've gotta be very,
very careful in that life,

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:44.130
if too many people get involved

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:45.470
everything goes up in smoke.

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:46.510
It happens all the time.

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:47.520
So when I went to him

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:49.520
I told him, I said,
"Junior, called him Junior,

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:51.677
I said, "Look, I'm gonna show more money

00:14:51.677 --> 00:14:53.530
"than you over saw in your life."

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:54.587
And he looked at me right away,

00:14:54.587 --> 00:14:56.030
"It's not drugs, we don't do drugs."

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:57.074
I said, "It's not drugs,

00:14:57.074 --> 00:14:59.290
"you know, I hate drugs,
personally I hate drugs."

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.760
Had it in my family.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:02.280
I said, "It's gas."

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:03.800
I said, "You're not gonna understand it,"

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:06.627
I said, "But I got this
operation under control,

00:15:06.627 --> 00:15:08.057
"nobody else is gonna be at risk.

00:15:08.057 --> 00:15:11.117
"It's me, my guys, my crew,
but I'll make you wealthy.

00:15:11.117 --> 00:15:12.597
"But here's the deal.

00:15:12.597 --> 00:15:14.677
"Every time we have a
sit down," excuse me,

00:15:14.677 --> 00:15:16.927
"an argument with another
family, I've got to win.

00:15:16.927 --> 00:15:19.787
"Don't play politics, let's
not spread this around,

00:15:19.787 --> 00:15:22.037
"'cause as soon as we do
it'll get out of control

00:15:22.037 --> 00:15:23.360
"and we'll blow it."

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.280
And he said, "Show me."

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:26.730
And I did.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.653
And I never lost an argument.

00:15:29.813 --> 00:15:32.660
I made him wealthy and he repaid me

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.610
by being loyal in that regard (coughs).

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:38.170
- [Mark] How many years did this last?

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:42.540
- Close to eight years from
'78, you know, right through '85

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.050
when I went to prison.

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:46.573
- [Mark] And what kind of
lifestyle did that afforded you?

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.080
- Well, I had my own jet plane,

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:51.923
I had a Lear 25A, I had a Bell helicopter,

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.810
I built a 8,000 square
foot house in Long Island,

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:57.800
I had a house in Florida, I had a house

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:00.350
in Marina Del Rey, California.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.690
So, I mean, I had all those little perks.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.200
But, you know, honestly
he plane and helicopter

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.390
were really business, I mean, I use them

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:08.790
you know, quite extensively.

00:16:09.758 --> 00:16:12.200
But, you know, I, look,
I enjoyed the fruits

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.033
of having that kind of money.

00:16:13.033 --> 00:16:15.670
- [Mark] I'm sure you're
meeting all kinds of dignitaries

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:18.610
and celebrities and
you're running in a circle

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.680
that's very, very, very different, right?

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:22.513
- Yeah.

00:16:22.513 --> 00:16:26.010
I mean, I had, you know,
associations with people that had

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:29.280
you know, good celebrity
connections, so got involved

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:32.440
with that to a great degree,
and, you know, life was good.

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:33.480
Of course, on the other side

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:35.320
I'm fighting the government
every day of my life.

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:37.740
- [Mark] Yeah, so at some point

00:16:40.155 --> 00:16:42.410
during this heyday of the gas business

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:43.710
that you were involved in,

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:47.870
somebody got suspicious,
that you were, kind of,

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.552
keeping more of the money than you

00:16:50.552 --> 00:16:53.073
should've been for yourself
and pulled you into a meeting.

00:16:53.073 --> 00:16:54.840
- Yeah. You know, when you're
making that kind of money,

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.110
you know, people they're
watching you, you know,

00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:58.420
it's kind of a double-edged sword.

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:00.263
And, you know, I was a younger guy,

00:17:00.263 --> 00:17:02.010
I had been appointed to captain, you know,

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:04.213
they made me a caporegime, Persico go did,

00:17:06.227 --> 00:17:07.830
and I had a big crew, had all the Russians

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.080
that were very loyal to me,

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:10.780
making a tremendous amount of money.

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:12.270
- [Mark] You were still young?

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:14.750
- Yeah, I was in my 20s, late 20s.

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:16.990
And, you know, there was a publication,

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:18.810
I think it was "Newsday,"
I'm not positive,

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:20.670
I don't remember now, but wrote a story

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:23.540
that I was becoming powerful
enough to break away

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.460
from the Colombos and start my own family.

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:28.080
It was fiction, had no
truth to it whatsoever,

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.880
but that was one reporter's take on it.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.460
So, you know, that gets
into people's heads,

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:34.730
you know, people start to wonder.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:37.060
I think Persico got a
little bit, you know,

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:38.150
suspicious of that,

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.270
so started to send some people around

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:43.180
to talk to my Russian connections
and so on and so forth.

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:46.190
So, you know, I'd watch
myself at that point

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:49.750
and I had no interest in, you
know, taking over families.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.660
As a matter of fact,
I'll be honest with you,

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:53.940
I hated going down to the social clubs

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:56.370
and being stuck in Brooklyn
when I can get on my plane

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:59.030
and go to Florida,
California, and, you know,

00:17:59.030 --> 00:17:59.910
enjoy the good life.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.810
That's what I was into.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.550
You know, when you're a
captain in that family

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:05.760
it's a lot of work 'cause
you've got guys under you

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:07.440
that are constantly getting in trouble,

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.430
constantly needing you,
you've got to sit down,

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:10.810
you've gotta be arguing all the time.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.370
I mean, you know, I mean

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:15.270
I enjoyed the life and I
was as much a part of it

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:18.210
as anybody, but I also
liked the good life.

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:20.630
So, I had things that
people used to say to me,

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:22.500
I used to go out to California a lot here,

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:25.090
and people used to tell
me, "How is it out there?"

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:26.290
I didn't want anybody to follow me,

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.267
so I'd say, "Oh, it's horrible.

00:18:27.267 --> 00:18:29.430
"Those people, it's terrible,

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:30.633
"you don't ever want to go out there."

00:18:30.633 --> 00:18:31.466
'Cause I didn't want anybody to come out.

00:18:31.466 --> 00:18:33.030
Meanwhile, I loved it, right.

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:34.430
Same with Florida, you know,

00:18:36.432 --> 00:18:38.520
so I had to watch myself and, you know,

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:39.780
I was on my guard and I knew it,

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:41.660
so I was careful.

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:45.083
- [Mark] Yeah, and then how
did it finally come to an end?

00:18:47.382 --> 00:18:48.215
- How did I come to an end?

00:18:48.215 --> 00:18:50.990
- [Mark] No, no the, I
mean you got into trouble

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:53.100
with the government, right?

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:55.890
- Well, I became a major
target of law enforcement.

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:56.780
I mean, I was--

00:18:57.618 --> 00:18:58.451
- [Mark] I would imagine
the government is like

00:18:58.451 --> 00:19:00.537
"What the hell is going on with (laughs)?"

00:19:01.374 --> 00:19:02.207
- Yeah.
- Something's not.

00:19:02.207 --> 00:19:03.610
- I mean, I had, I total it up,

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:06.030
I had seven indictments, you know,

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:08.690
that's almost a record, you
know, I mean in that life.

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.648
Usually get one or two
and you're gone, you know,

00:19:10.648 --> 00:19:12.690
(chuckles), but I had seven,

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.777
and two federal racketeering cases.

00:19:14.777 --> 00:19:16.160
- [Mark] Rudy Giuliani was after you.

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:19.400
- Giuliani indicted me
on a big case in '84

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:21.410
I was probably the first major mob guy

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.850
he indicted under the RICO statute

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:26.150
and I was lead defendant,
I had 15 co-defendants

00:19:28.244 --> 00:19:30.144
and I was on trial for several months.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.580
If I lose that case, I'm gone, you know

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.003
I would have been away for 50, 100 years.

00:19:36.003 --> 00:19:39.370
- [Mark] At that point they
were putting guys away probably.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:42.290
- You know, I'm watching
these guys going to trial

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:47.160
getting convicted and
getting 100 years, 200 years.

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:48.997
I said, "Man, I'm the youngest
out of all of these guys

00:19:48.997 --> 00:19:51.970
"they're going to give me 500
years if I lose this case."

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:55.210
So, you know, I prepared day and night

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:57.280
for the Giuliani case.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.550
- [Mark] How much money
did you spend on lawyers?

00:20:00.538 --> 00:20:03.430
- In all total, probably
about $2.5 million, you know,

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:07.230
between all the cases,
you know, I took care

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:11.200
of some of my co-defendants
and investigators, you know,

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:12.950
then forget the hours that I lost,

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:15.198
just, you know, preparing.

00:20:15.198 --> 00:20:17.510
But yeah, I spent a lot of
money, but it was worth it.

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:20.270
I mean, I won the case, I was acquitted.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:22.030
So got my freedom.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.363
At least at that point.

00:20:23.363 --> 00:20:25.770
- [Mark] You escaped the
government several times, right?

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.840
- Yeah, I beat them five times.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:31.020
I went to trial three times,

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:33.740
fourth time was dismissed and
Giuliani, I was acquitted.

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:36.113
I got, I had a pretty good string.

00:20:37.737 --> 00:20:39.120
- [Mark] Now you were also involved

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:41.550
in sports gambling as well, is that right?

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:42.870
- Well, you know, if you're in that life

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.400
you're into gambling in some way.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.820
Now I didn't have that habit.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:46.750
I used to gamble a little bit

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:49.060
on sports, I played the numbers every day,

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:51.350
5, 27, my birthday, won a few times.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.640
But we had bookmakers that answered

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:56.620
to me and they were gambling,

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.650
I mean, athletes were
gambling with them, you know,

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:01.360
all the time, all the major sports teams,

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.973
a lot of the college kids,
you know, just happening.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:07.580
- [Mark] Michael Jordan
was apparently involved

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:10.220
in some mess with the--.

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:12.807
- Well, look, it was on the street,

00:21:12.807 --> 00:21:14.480
and everybody knew who Michael was,

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:16.970
I only use the word degenerate
in terms of his gambling

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:19.690
not in terms of him personally,
but he was, he was hard.

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:20.600
It's still today.

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:23.453
I mean, everybody now
he's not shy about it.

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:28.030
Yeah, but he was gambling
with bookmakers, you know,

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:29.133
we were aware of it.

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:36.653
- [Mark] So what happens after,

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:40.560
you actually did do
some prison time, right?

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:43.140
- Yeah, what happened after
I beat the Giuliani case,

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:45.250
the East that was in the
Southern District of New York

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:46.780
and then the Eastern District of New York

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:50.760
was preparing this whole
gasoline tax RICO case on me.

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:52.860
It was kind of a laundry list of things

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:57.090
they indicted me for,
but you know, gasoline

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:57.923
was one of them.

00:21:57.923 --> 00:22:00.470
And the guy that introduced
me, Larry Iorizzo

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:03.170
to the business, and then we
created the scheme together,

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:04.890
he turned informant.

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:07.730
So he was their principal
witness against me.

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:12.120
However, he testified against
me in the Giuliani case

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:15.490
and we destroyed hin on
the stand, destroyed him.

00:22:15.490 --> 00:22:17.550
So the government was
leery about him coming in

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:19.730
on the second case, which
gave me some leverage

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:21.823
when I finally negotiated a plea there.

00:22:23.620 --> 00:22:26.080
- [Mark] So a plea got you how many years?

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:28.940
- I took a plea eventually
to a 10 year prison sentence.

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:33.940
I had a $15 million in
forfeitures and restitution.

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:37.630
And I gave up the plane,
the helicopter the whole bit

00:22:37.630 --> 00:22:39.050
and went off to do my time.

00:22:39.050 --> 00:22:42.370
But you got to understand at
that time, when I got 10 years

00:22:42.370 --> 00:22:44.727
I negotiated it for
months, people were saying,

00:22:44.727 --> 00:22:46.340
"Hey, it's a deal of the century."

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:47.173
- [Mark] You got off easy.

00:22:47.173 --> 00:22:48.006
- Yeah, they would telling me,

00:22:48.006 --> 00:22:48.839
"Don't even take your shoes off,

00:22:48.839 --> 00:22:50.940
"you'll be home before
you know it, really."

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:52.750
But that's how bad it was back then.

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:54.660
So I was very fortunate.

00:22:54.660 --> 00:22:59.480
- [Mark] No, I find it very
interesting that you have

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:05.420
navigated your time with
the mob and your life today

00:23:05.420 --> 00:23:08.563
with, I think it's,

00:23:09.710 --> 00:23:11.440
people have many different
types of intelligence,

00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:15.510
but there's a wisdom in knowing

00:23:19.597 --> 00:23:21.300
how to play a certain
situation or a certain person

00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:24.233
you're interacting with
to come out on top,

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:26.580
to come out unscathed,

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:28.917
and compared to, like on that list of

00:23:28.917 --> 00:23:31.163
"Fortune the 50 Mob Bosses"

00:23:32.376 --> 00:23:34.880
(laughs) I think you're the
only one who's still alive

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:36.260
or still not in prison?

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:40.120
- Well, no, no, I know
48 of them are dead.

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:41.620
I don't know about the 49th.

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:44.090
I heard he's in his '70s,
he might've passed away.

00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:46.030
I know he was doing a long prison stretch,

00:23:46.030 --> 00:23:48.110
I don't know where he is.

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:50.670
So yeah, I mean, I'm the guy
that's walking around free.

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:52.900
I mean, it's, you know, look, I always say

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:54.310
that list was kind of silly.

00:23:54.310 --> 00:23:56.050
They didn't ask for our
tax returns, you know,

00:23:56.050 --> 00:23:57.200
they'd make a list like that.

00:23:57.200 --> 00:23:59.080
Sold a lot of magazines.

00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:01.790
But you know, it's not silly
even to myself is to think

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:06.120
that over the last 33 years,
I survived all of these guys.

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:10.410
I mean, it makes me realize how fortunate

00:24:10.410 --> 00:24:12.612
and blessed I am, you know, to know that.

00:24:12.612 --> 00:24:15.830
This whole thing, you know,
it was all in negotiation,

00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:17.593
life is a negotiation.

00:24:18.513 --> 00:24:20.362
And when it came to this next case

00:24:20.362 --> 00:24:23.000
that they were after me on,

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:26.810
I knew I had a shot when we
defeated their major witness

00:24:26.810 --> 00:24:29.310
in the Giuliani case,
they were devastated.

00:24:29.310 --> 00:24:30.297
And so I told my lawyer,

00:24:30.297 --> 00:24:32.317
"Look, I can't keep fighting these people

00:24:32.317 --> 00:24:33.397
"eventually they're gonna win,

00:24:33.397 --> 00:24:36.000
"and when they do win,
I'm going away forever."

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:38.120
I said, "I've got to
try to cut my losses."

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:40.210
So in taking that plea,

00:24:40.210 --> 00:24:41.810
what I really was concerned about,

00:24:41.810 --> 00:24:43.590
look, I wasn't afraid to do the jail time.

00:24:43.590 --> 00:24:45.370
I was visiting my father my whole life,

00:24:45.370 --> 00:24:47.530
I knew at some point
I'd do some prison time,

00:24:47.530 --> 00:24:49.913
I had 17 or 18 arrests up to that point.

00:24:51.755 --> 00:24:53.110
but I said, "I've got to cut my losses."

00:24:53.110 --> 00:24:55.550
And what was more important
to me than anything else

00:24:55.550 --> 00:24:57.960
was getting immunity
from any other crimes.

00:24:57.960 --> 00:25:00.930
So I knew if I wrapped
everything up in that plea deal,

00:25:00.930 --> 00:25:03.630
I did a few, you know, years inside,

00:25:03.630 --> 00:25:05.890
I'd come out and have a clean slate.

00:25:05.890 --> 00:25:08.810
And they gave me immunity
for everything except murder,

00:25:08.810 --> 00:25:09.740
you know, at that time

00:25:09.740 --> 00:25:11.530
unless I became a cooperating witness

00:25:11.530 --> 00:25:14.505
then they would have given
me immunity for murder,

00:25:14.505 --> 00:25:15.360
but I wasn't interested in that.

00:25:15.360 --> 00:25:17.250
So that was the only thing
I had to be concerned about,

00:25:17.250 --> 00:25:19.200
and I wasn't really concerned about it.

00:25:20.210 --> 00:25:23.590
And so it was really a
negotiation to preserve

00:25:23.590 --> 00:25:26.020
the rest of my life and get
these people off my back.

00:25:26.020 --> 00:25:27.040
That's what it was all about.

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:30.360
- [Mark] Did you have
an eye on getting away

00:25:30.360 --> 00:25:32.150
from a mob life at that point?

00:25:32.150 --> 00:25:34.540
- I did, you know, a couple of things

00:25:34.540 --> 00:25:37.040
came into to the question for me,

00:25:37.040 --> 00:25:40.800
but I saw that that life
was in a lot of trouble.

00:25:40.800 --> 00:25:43.470
I mean, Giuliani, I have to
give them credit or blame

00:25:43.470 --> 00:25:44.860
whatever way you look at it, you know,

00:25:44.860 --> 00:25:47.820
for really utilizing the RICO Act.

00:25:47.820 --> 00:25:49.890
And up until I'd point, you know,

00:25:49.890 --> 00:25:52.810
guys weren't becoming as
informants much as they were,

00:25:52.810 --> 00:25:54.837
but nobody wanted to
face that kind of time.

00:25:54.837 --> 00:25:58.390
And I saw the life starting
to fall apart because of that,

00:25:58.390 --> 00:26:00.740
the government had too many weapons.

00:26:00.740 --> 00:26:03.486
They had the RICO Act, they
had the Bail Reform act,

00:26:03.486 --> 00:26:04.730
the had the Sentencing Reform Act.

00:26:04.730 --> 00:26:06.560
Guys would turning snitch left and right.

00:26:06.560 --> 00:26:08.300
- [Mark] Better surveillance.

00:26:08.300 --> 00:26:09.150
- What's that?

00:26:09.150 --> 00:26:09.983
- [Mark] Better surveillance.

00:26:09.983 --> 00:26:11.270
- Yeah, better surveillance.

00:26:11.270 --> 00:26:13.120
And we didn't keep up with the times,

00:26:14.322 --> 00:26:15.517
and so I said, "This life is in trouble.

00:26:15.517 --> 00:26:18.557
"If you're gonna stay
here, and I'm a young guy,

00:26:18.557 --> 00:26:20.160
"for me to be arrogant enough to think

00:26:20.160 --> 00:26:21.847
"that over the course of my lifetime,

00:26:21.847 --> 00:26:23.767
"these guys wouldn't catch me in something

00:26:23.767 --> 00:26:25.960
"and put me away forever would have been

00:26:25.960 --> 00:26:26.980
arrogant on my part."

00:26:26.980 --> 00:26:28.126
- [Mark] Yeah, so you knew something

00:26:28.126 --> 00:26:29.286
was gonna be happening.

00:26:29.286 --> 00:26:31.230
10 years is nothing compared--

00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:33.620
- 10 years was, I did eight on the 10,

00:26:33.620 --> 00:26:35.830
but it was, you know, it was a blessing.

00:26:35.830 --> 00:26:37.660
- [Mark] If you look at
everyone else around you,

00:26:37.660 --> 00:26:40.904
you got off easier than anybody
in the history of anyone.

00:26:40.904 --> 00:26:44.980
- Absolutely, and didn't have
to put anybody in prison.

00:26:44.980 --> 00:26:46.750
Didn't go into witness protection program,

00:26:46.750 --> 00:26:48.893
none of that, which I
wasn't interested in.

00:26:49.923 --> 00:26:51.640
Everybody said it was unheard of,

00:26:51.640 --> 00:26:53.470
it's never been done before.

00:26:53.470 --> 00:26:55.260
I mean, I don't do research on it,

00:26:55.260 --> 00:26:57.890
but I don't know of anybody
else that's been that fortunate,

00:26:57.890 --> 00:26:59.210
Lets' put it that way.
- What was the reaction

00:26:59.210 --> 00:27:02.050
to other mobsters at the time,

00:27:02.050 --> 00:27:04.260
when you were kind of leaving?

00:27:04.260 --> 00:27:05.093
- Well, they didn't know it.

00:27:05.093 --> 00:27:06.750
I mean, I didn't make an announcement.

00:27:06.750 --> 00:27:08.430
- [Mark] But at some point you--

00:27:08.430 --> 00:27:09.950
- Well, I'll tell you what happened.

00:27:09.950 --> 00:27:14.190
When I went into prison,
I was in there for a bit,

00:27:14.190 --> 00:27:17.560
and the associate warden
at Terminal Island,

00:27:17.560 --> 00:27:20.087
that's where I was incarcerated, tells me,

00:27:20.087 --> 00:27:23.447
"You know, 'Life Magazine's'
doing this huge story on you,"

00:27:24.538 --> 00:27:26.110
they had done a huge story on
my dad several years earlier,

00:27:26.110 --> 00:27:28.523
it was actually the biggest story ever,

00:27:29.905 --> 00:27:32.010
as far as I know in "Life
Magazine" about my dad.

00:27:32.010 --> 00:27:35.443
It was like 29 pages with
photos and everything else.

00:27:36.341 --> 00:27:37.200
So he said they're doing, kind of,

00:27:37.200 --> 00:27:38.963
an anniversary edition on you,

00:27:40.064 --> 00:27:41.527
and he said, "The reporter
said if you speak to them,

00:27:41.527 --> 00:27:43.220
"it'll be a better story."

00:27:43.220 --> 00:27:45.290
So me always trying to negotiate stuff,

00:27:45.290 --> 00:27:46.607
I said, "All right, maybe
I get the government

00:27:46.607 --> 00:27:48.427
"off my back a little
bit, you know, whatever,

00:27:48.427 --> 00:27:50.340
"get out of here, get some peace."

00:27:50.340 --> 00:27:52.040
So I sit down with him
and I said, you know

00:27:52.040 --> 00:27:53.717
I tell them typical mob stuff.

00:27:53.717 --> 00:27:55.618
"There is no mob,

00:27:55.618 --> 00:27:56.767
"I don't know what you're talking about.

00:27:56.767 --> 00:27:58.977
"I married this young girl,
she's from California,

00:27:58.977 --> 00:27:59.810
"I moved out.

00:27:59.810 --> 00:28:00.860
"I liked the sunny weather."

00:28:00.860 --> 00:28:02.761
I gave him all that stuff.

00:28:02.761 --> 00:28:03.940
And that was it.

00:28:03.940 --> 00:28:05.080
I think a couple of weeks later

00:28:05.080 --> 00:28:06.160
the warden calls me back

00:28:06.160 --> 00:28:07.307
to the office and he says,

00:28:07.307 --> 00:28:09.400
"Franzese, do you have a death wish?

00:28:09.400 --> 00:28:10.770
I said, "What are you talking about?"

00:28:10.770 --> 00:28:12.590
He shows me the article.

00:28:12.590 --> 00:28:15.210
It was a big, double
picture, a big article,

00:28:15.210 --> 00:28:17.790
and across the top, "Quitting the Mafia,"

00:28:17.790 --> 00:28:19.180
and there's a big picture of me.

00:28:19.180 --> 00:28:21.090
And I'm in jail with
several other mob guys.

00:28:21.090 --> 00:28:22.975
This guy had me doing
everything but testifying.

00:28:22.975 --> 00:28:23.936
- [Mark] Nobody leaves the mob.

00:28:23.936 --> 00:28:25.573
- No.
- Not that way (laughs).

00:28:25.573 --> 00:28:26.490
- No.

00:28:26.490 --> 00:28:27.830
And then right after that, you know,

00:28:27.830 --> 00:28:29.540
I get a visit from the government.

00:28:29.540 --> 00:28:31.497
FBI tells me, "Hey,
words all over the street

00:28:31.497 --> 00:28:35.190
"from our informants,
'You're a dead man, anyway,'

00:28:35.190 --> 00:28:37.790
cooperate with us, we'll
put you in a program.

00:28:37.790 --> 00:28:41.410
And so this thing started
like accidentally, you know,

00:28:41.410 --> 00:28:43.400
I didn't say I was
testifying against anybody

00:28:43.400 --> 00:28:45.390
but then they put word out on the street

00:28:45.390 --> 00:28:46.660
that I was gonna testify.

00:28:46.660 --> 00:28:49.246
They put my name on the witness list

00:28:49.246 --> 00:28:50.780
of other trials that were going up.

00:28:50.780 --> 00:28:51.840
So people were seeing that

00:28:51.840 --> 00:28:54.590
on the discovery, was like
a wave that I couldn't stop.

00:28:56.135 --> 00:28:58.813
But I did have no intention of going back,

00:28:58.813 --> 00:29:00.210
so messages came through
to me, "What's up?"

00:29:00.210 --> 00:29:02.047
I said, "Look, I'm not gonna hurt anybody,

00:29:02.047 --> 00:29:03.280
"but I'm done&gt;"

00:29:03.280 --> 00:29:07.640
Well, that infuriated the wrong
people, including my father.

00:29:07.640 --> 00:29:08.829
So, I mean, I had a lot of
trouble, a lot of trouble.

00:29:08.829 --> 00:29:12.060
- [Mark] Yeah, your dad
actually spoke against you.

00:29:12.060 --> 00:29:14.500
- You know, I'd like to clarify that.

00:29:14.500 --> 00:29:16.850
I mean, obviously the contract on my life,

00:29:16.850 --> 00:29:21.100
Persico, very upset when
he heard this and I'm done,

00:29:21.100 --> 00:29:22.630
plus they thought I was gonna testify,

00:29:22.630 --> 00:29:24.460
so, you know, I was told straight out

00:29:24.460 --> 00:29:26.180
my father went along with the contract.

00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:31.083
And, you know, knowing
my dad, I believed it.

00:29:32.170 --> 00:29:35.290
I don't think my dad would
have pulled the trigger on me,

00:29:35.290 --> 00:29:36.140
but he let it go.

00:29:37.380 --> 00:29:38.590
- [Mark] But I think it's a testament

00:29:38.590 --> 00:29:40.630
to your wisdom to navigate

00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:45.898
negative things like that, your own father

00:29:45.898 --> 00:29:49.340
kind of standing against you and yet

00:29:50.660 --> 00:29:52.790
using it, and finding
some way to turn that

00:29:52.790 --> 00:29:54.592
into something positive.

00:29:54.592 --> 00:29:57.070
And your relationship with
your dad is still alive?

00:29:57.070 --> 00:29:57.903
- [Michael] Yes.

00:29:57.903 --> 00:29:59.347
- [Mark] Just got out of
prison recently, right?

00:29:59.347 --> 00:30:01.286
- [Michael] My dad's still
alive, he's 102 years old.

00:30:01.286 --> 00:30:02.119
- [Mark[ 102.

00:30:02.119 --> 00:30:04.220
- [Michael] He was
released at the age of 100.

00:30:05.203 --> 00:30:06.780
He was the oldest inmate in the system.

00:30:06.780 --> 00:30:08.720
- [Mark] I'm sure your
relationship with him is great.

00:30:08.720 --> 00:30:10.920
- [Michael] It's, you know, it's good.

00:30:10.920 --> 00:30:14.150
You know, we kind of see
things a little bit differently

00:30:14.150 --> 00:30:18.330
at this point, you know, but
the relationship is good.

00:30:18.330 --> 00:30:19.163
I love my dad.

00:30:19.163 --> 00:30:20.320
He loves me.

00:30:20.320 --> 00:30:21.840
You know, there's a lot of talk out there

00:30:21.840 --> 00:30:22.800
and all this stuff.

00:30:22.800 --> 00:30:24.290
I never did anything to hurt my dad.

00:30:24.290 --> 00:30:25.960
I only tried to help him my whole life.

00:30:25.960 --> 00:30:27.820
I'm the guy that got him
out of prison, you know,

00:30:27.820 --> 00:30:29.179
and all these times.

00:30:29.179 --> 00:30:31.440
But, you know, people
talk and they like to say

00:30:31.440 --> 00:30:33.930
certain things and
whatever, but my dad and I

00:30:33.930 --> 00:30:36.850
are close and, you know,
I love him, he loves me.

00:30:36.850 --> 00:30:38.310
- [Mark] That's great.

00:30:38.310 --> 00:30:40.830
And he was a big influence
in your, who you are, right?

00:30:40.830 --> 00:30:42.620
- [Michael] My dad was a
tremendous influence on me.

00:30:42.620 --> 00:30:45.330
He taught me, you know,
all the right things

00:30:45.330 --> 00:30:46.480
when I was a kid growing up,

00:30:46.480 --> 00:30:48.703
I believe I still carry that with me.

00:30:48.703 --> 00:30:51.310
He helped me navigate through that life,

00:30:51.310 --> 00:30:52.860
taught me to be a good listener, you know,

00:30:52.860 --> 00:30:56.190
to be be careful before
I speak out of turn,

00:30:56.190 --> 00:30:57.760
and things that you need
to know in that life

00:30:57.760 --> 00:30:59.202
that are very important.

00:30:59.202 --> 00:31:00.220
"Cause guys that shoot off their mouth

00:31:00.220 --> 00:31:02.600
and wanted to be tough
guys, they're all gone.

00:31:02.600 --> 00:31:03.433
You don't keep somebody that around

00:31:03.433 --> 00:31:05.787
when you got to worry about
somebody doing to you,

00:31:05.787 --> 00:31:08.280
you let them go, you
know, get rid of them,

00:31:08.280 --> 00:31:09.113
and that's what happened.

00:31:09.113 --> 00:31:11.170
I saw that happened
many times in that life.

00:31:12.920 --> 00:31:14.090
- [Mark] Tell me about
some of the personalities.

00:31:14.090 --> 00:31:15.860
I'm sure you came across (chuckles)

00:31:15.860 --> 00:31:17.730
quite a few real characters.

00:31:17.730 --> 00:31:18.680
Gotti, for example.

00:31:19.570 --> 00:31:22.240
- Yeah, you know, I was
friendly with John, you know,

00:31:22.240 --> 00:31:23.570
we weren't best of friends,

00:31:23.570 --> 00:31:25.120
had different crews and all of that.

00:31:25.120 --> 00:31:27.960
I had my run-ins with him with Gotti.

00:31:27.960 --> 00:31:29.730
Socially, he was great,

00:31:29.730 --> 00:31:31.270
I used to meet him in
some clubs, you know,

00:31:31.270 --> 00:31:34.080
by chance or on purpose, we'd
have a drink and have fun,

00:31:34.080 --> 00:31:34.980
he was great.

00:31:34.980 --> 00:31:37.310
He was always had to be like
the center of attention.

00:31:37.310 --> 00:31:39.746
He was the magnet, everybody,
'cause the way he dressed,

00:31:39.746 --> 00:31:42.062
the way he carried himself.

00:31:42.062 --> 00:31:44.140
But, was a lot of fun.

00:31:44.140 --> 00:31:47.030
Business, very tough, very, very tough

00:31:47.030 --> 00:31:48.797
'cause, you know, he had the attitude

00:31:48.797 --> 00:31:50.750
"I'm John Gotti and
nobody's gonna beat me."

00:31:50.750 --> 00:31:53.250
And so when you in a deal with him

00:31:53.250 --> 00:31:55.450
whether it be purposely or by chance

00:31:55.450 --> 00:31:57.900
you had to know how to
navigate your way through.

00:31:57.900 --> 00:31:59.330
so he thinks he got what he wanted

00:31:59.330 --> 00:32:01.860
but actually you get what you want.

00:32:01.860 --> 00:32:04.630
And I appreciate, 'cause
John doesn't know it,

00:32:04.630 --> 00:32:06.990
but he taught me that just in
my having to deal with him,

00:32:06.990 --> 00:32:09.130
you know, and getting my way at the end.

00:32:09.130 --> 00:32:10.880
- [Mark] Yeah, well, I
mean, you can be headstrong

00:32:10.880 --> 00:32:15.880
or you can be wise and you
know, one gets you further.

00:32:15.880 --> 00:32:17.463
- You get the credit, I'll take the money.

00:32:17.463 --> 00:32:19.140
It's that way.

00:32:19.140 --> 00:32:22.650
- [Mark] Who else, what other mob figures

00:32:22.650 --> 00:32:25.060
were particularly
interesting to deal with?

00:32:25.060 --> 00:32:28.417
- Well, you know, I enjoyed Tony Salerno,

00:32:28.417 --> 00:32:30.740
"Fat Tony" Salerno was the
boss of the Genovese family.

00:32:30.740 --> 00:32:32.140
He was a character, you know,

00:32:32.140 --> 00:32:35.060
right out of central
casting, but a good guy,

00:32:35.060 --> 00:32:35.893
I liked him.

00:32:35.893 --> 00:32:36.950
I had a couple of, you know,

00:32:36.950 --> 00:32:38.990
meetings with him and
enjoyed him very much.

00:32:38.990 --> 00:32:40.730
In the gas business, especially, you know,

00:32:40.730 --> 00:32:42.980
he knew I was making money.

00:32:42.980 --> 00:32:44.217
He asked me for a couple of things

00:32:44.217 --> 00:32:45.593
and I was able to help him.

00:32:46.950 --> 00:32:50.250
Paul Castellano I met under
not great circumstances.

00:32:50.250 --> 00:32:53.530
My first real run-in where the guy was him

00:32:53.530 --> 00:32:56.670
and it didn't, you know, he
wasn't one of my favorite guys,

00:32:56.670 --> 00:32:58.120
let's put it that way.

00:32:58.120 --> 00:32:59.500
You know, Persico, obviously I knew.

00:32:59.500 --> 00:33:00.550
I mean, I knew a lot of guys,

00:33:00.550 --> 00:33:01.940
I mean, I got around, you know,

00:33:01.940 --> 00:33:04.633
I knew the Chin, you know,
fairly well, Chin Gigante.

00:33:05.540 --> 00:33:08.740
He really was the most powerful guy

00:33:08.740 --> 00:33:11.660
on the street at that point
in time, he really was.

00:33:11.660 --> 00:33:13.810
I mean, you know, he
did his thing, you know,

00:33:13.810 --> 00:33:16.140
walking up and down Houston
Street, in the bathroom

00:33:16.140 --> 00:33:16.973
and all of that.

00:33:16.973 --> 00:33:18.260
But very interesting,

00:33:18.260 --> 00:33:20.330
he didn't care who you
were, he didn't care,

00:33:20.330 --> 00:33:21.500
you could be the boss of another family,

00:33:21.500 --> 00:33:22.333
he didn't care.

00:33:22.333 --> 00:33:24.300
If he didn't wanna meet you
or talk to you he wouldn't.

00:33:24.300 --> 00:33:26.290
And the fact that he
met with me, you know,

00:33:26.290 --> 00:33:30.490
on a few occasions and
treated me that way was nice.

00:33:30.490 --> 00:33:32.010
He respected my father a lot too.

00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:34.740
My father was away, but he respected him.

00:33:34.740 --> 00:33:36.490
So I met, you know, I met the good guys

00:33:36.490 --> 00:33:39.210
the top guys at the time and
I met a lot of the other guys

00:33:39.210 --> 00:33:40.890
you know, because you're in a gas business

00:33:40.890 --> 00:33:43.950
everybody wanted a piece of it, everybody.

00:33:43.950 --> 00:33:45.750
So I was constantly sitting down

00:33:45.750 --> 00:33:47.963
and keeping people away and arguing.

00:33:49.077 --> 00:33:52.170
It was a lot of work,
but it was profitable,

00:33:52.170 --> 00:33:53.300
so you did the work.

00:33:53.300 --> 00:33:57.250
- Right. And Giuliani, did
you have a lot of interactions

00:33:57.250 --> 00:33:58.523
with Rudy Giuliani?

00:33:59.850 --> 00:34:02.370
- No, not a lot, but you
know, day of my arraignment

00:34:02.370 --> 00:34:05.100
he told me if he convicted me,
he's gonna give me 100 years,

00:34:05.100 --> 00:34:06.403
double what my father got.

00:34:07.357 --> 00:34:08.325
And I said, "Hey, bring it on Rudy.

00:34:08.325 --> 00:34:11.810
"Beat you already four times,
let's go for round five."

00:34:11.810 --> 00:34:13.610
And fortunately I beat him.

00:34:13.610 --> 00:34:16.780
But, you know, Rudy said some nice things

00:34:16.780 --> 00:34:20.350
about me when it was out on
the street that, you know,

00:34:20.350 --> 00:34:24.107
I was transforming my life
and I was not going back.

00:34:24.107 --> 00:34:25.517
And everybody was saying,

00:34:25.517 --> 00:34:27.847
"Franzese is full of it,"
on law enforcement side.

00:34:27.847 --> 00:34:28.987
"He'll never give this up.

00:34:28.987 --> 00:34:30.427
"He's too much a part of it.

00:34:30.427 --> 00:34:32.600
"It's another scam he's pulling."

00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:34.727
And Giuliani said, "You know what?

00:34:34.727 --> 00:34:36.567
"Michael's a fairly intelligent guy

00:34:36.567 --> 00:34:38.497
"and he knows his life is in trouble,

00:34:38.497 --> 00:34:41.010
"and I think he might be
sincere in what he's saying."

00:34:41.010 --> 00:34:42.030
He made that comment.

00:34:42.030 --> 00:34:43.620
So, it was nice.

00:34:43.620 --> 00:34:45.010
- [Mark] It's interesting.

00:34:45.010 --> 00:34:48.160
It takes intelligence to
recognize intelligence, sometimes.

00:34:48.160 --> 00:34:50.390
- Well, look, like I said, and you wanna

00:34:50.390 --> 00:34:52.460
give him the credit or
the blame, but, you know,

00:34:52.460 --> 00:34:56.230
he did a lot as far as
hurting my former life.

00:34:56.230 --> 00:34:59.880
And I will say this, I think
he was a terrific mayor.

00:34:59.880 --> 00:35:01.330
I'll tell you a story.

00:35:01.330 --> 00:35:03.990
You know, I had been, I did my five years,

00:35:03.990 --> 00:35:06.980
I was out 13 months, violated my parole,

00:35:06.980 --> 00:35:08.920
so they picked me up and
they're bringing me back

00:35:08.920 --> 00:35:11.880
to New York, I was out in California

00:35:11.880 --> 00:35:13.980
because I had to go in front of the judge,

00:35:15.790 --> 00:35:18.067
the marshals were
transporting me and I said,

00:35:18.067 --> 00:35:20.860
"Look, what time we gotta be at court?"

00:35:20.860 --> 00:35:21.880
He said like two o'clock.

00:35:21.880 --> 00:35:23.350
It was early in the morning,
we got off the plane.

00:35:23.350 --> 00:35:24.657
I said, "Well, do me a favor.

00:35:24.657 --> 00:35:25.727
"I haven't been here for a while.

00:35:25.727 --> 00:35:28.380
"Let's drive around Manhattan,
I wanna see what's going on."

00:35:28.380 --> 00:35:29.927
I said, "That and I want Dunkin' Donuts.

00:35:29.927 --> 00:35:31.150
"I haven't had that in a while too."

00:35:31.150 --> 00:35:32.850
So the marshals were good guys.

00:35:32.850 --> 00:35:35.330
So we started driving
around, we go to Manhattan

00:35:35.330 --> 00:35:38.640
and I was shocked to see Times Square.

00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:41.920
I grew up, Time Square was
a pit, it was horrible.

00:35:41.920 --> 00:35:42.757
- [Mark] You wouldn't walk there.

00:35:42.757 --> 00:35:45.610
- No, and Giuliani totally transformed it.

00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:48.300
So, you know, he did a lot
of good things as mayor,

00:35:48.300 --> 00:35:50.980
and, of course, 9/11, he
gets, you know, both sides,

00:35:50.980 --> 00:35:52.230
but I think he did a good job.

00:35:52.230 --> 00:35:53.853
So give him credit.

00:35:55.100 --> 00:35:57.580
- [Mark] So what are the qualities

00:35:57.580 --> 00:36:01.106
that a person needs to exist in that life?

00:36:01.106 --> 00:36:03.337
I mean, there's loyalty,
there's integrity and all that,

00:36:03.337 --> 00:36:06.640
but it seems like very
often it's the case where

00:36:06.640 --> 00:36:10.023
it's were deceit and treachery
come into the picture.

00:36:11.910 --> 00:36:14.230
- You know, it's a very treacherous life.

00:36:14.230 --> 00:36:17.120
And the reason I say that because look,

00:36:17.120 --> 00:36:19.220
I spent a lot of time
there, over 20 years.

00:36:19.220 --> 00:36:23.070
I mean, you know, I seen guys
die for the wrong reasons.

00:36:23.070 --> 00:36:25.140
Jealousy comes into effect.

00:36:25.140 --> 00:36:26.920
There's a lot of politics.

00:36:26.920 --> 00:36:29.180
Money is everything, money
and powers is everything

00:36:29.180 --> 00:36:30.530
in that life,

00:36:30.530 --> 00:36:33.800
and you've got to know how
to really navigate both.

00:36:33.800 --> 00:36:35.240
And if you're make good money

00:36:35.240 --> 00:36:36.855
and you have power, you've gotta know,

00:36:36.855 --> 00:36:38.710
you've gotta be careful.

00:36:38.710 --> 00:36:40.490
You don't wanna offend the wrong people,

00:36:40.490 --> 00:36:41.980
I mean, look, the Gotti, Castellano thing

00:36:41.980 --> 00:36:43.360
was a perfect example.

00:36:43.360 --> 00:36:46.970
In our family, "Little
Vic" Orena, you know,

00:36:46.970 --> 00:36:48.080
he went out against Persico,

00:36:48.080 --> 00:36:50.210
he had a big war at that time.

00:36:50.210 --> 00:36:53.420
So you've gotta be very careful in there.

00:36:53.420 --> 00:36:55.890
You've gotta be careful,
you know, just to do

00:36:55.890 --> 00:36:57.240
the right thing with the right people,

00:36:57.240 --> 00:36:59.820
or to be on your guard all the time.

00:36:59.820 --> 00:37:02.630
And, you know, again, I saw a lot

00:37:02.630 --> 00:37:04.350
of people die for the wrong reason.

00:37:04.350 --> 00:37:06.200
One of the horrors in that life,

00:37:06.200 --> 00:37:08.420
you make a mistake, your best friend walks

00:37:08.420 --> 00:37:11.100
you into a room, you don't walk out again.

00:37:11.100 --> 00:37:13.000
And unfortunately I've witnessed that.

00:37:14.120 --> 00:37:17.040
I had somebody very close to
me that I believe was killed

00:37:17.040 --> 00:37:18.430
for the wrong reasons,

00:37:18.430 --> 00:37:21.860
more to give me a message
than to anything else.

00:37:21.860 --> 00:37:25.060
And that was tough for me to get over.

00:37:25.060 --> 00:37:26.500
I mean, it really was 'cause things,

00:37:26.500 --> 00:37:30.560
look, you know, I'm not
throwing bouquets in myself

00:37:30.560 --> 00:37:34.120
and I'm no angel by any
means, but, you know

00:37:34.120 --> 00:37:36.440
I saw two types of guys in that life.

00:37:36.440 --> 00:37:39.460
There were guys there that I
would call them stone killers,

00:37:39.460 --> 00:37:40.557
they enjoyed it.

00:37:40.557 --> 00:37:42.437
"Hey, give me the
contract, "I'm ready to go,

00:37:42.437 --> 00:37:43.907
"I love it, and I'll do it."

00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:46.830
And they did it, they did their job.

00:37:46.830 --> 00:37:50.720
You know, for me, when I was
asked to order to do something

00:37:52.400 --> 00:37:54.010
it made me uncomfortable.

00:37:54.010 --> 00:37:56.633
And don't get me wrong, I
never let anybody see that,

00:37:57.515 --> 00:37:59.520
and, you know, I did what I
had to do and, and did it.

00:37:59.520 --> 00:38:03.960
And in my case it was kinda
like stepping outside of myself,

00:38:03.960 --> 00:38:06.620
doing what I had to do
and getting right back

00:38:06.620 --> 00:38:09.823
because I wasn't gonna
let anybody talk about me,

00:38:09.823 --> 00:38:12.320
and I was gonna make sure I
did what I was told to do,

00:38:12.320 --> 00:38:13.920
follow the orders.

00:38:13.920 --> 00:38:17.630
But I think there really
was those two type of guys,

00:38:17.630 --> 00:38:19.510
those two types of personalities.

00:38:19.510 --> 00:38:20.780
And I'll tell you this,

00:38:20.780 --> 00:38:23.940
the guys that were ready
to kill, they don't last.

00:38:23.940 --> 00:38:26.377
They don't last because people say,

00:38:26.377 --> 00:38:27.737
"I'm not gonna worry about this guy,

00:38:27.737 --> 00:38:29.740
"he's too quick with the trigger."

00:38:29.740 --> 00:38:33.090
You know, one thing that I
learned, if you're a captain

00:38:33.090 --> 00:38:36.660
in that family, and
wanna clear this up too,

00:38:36.660 --> 00:38:39.380
murder was taken very
seriously in that life,

00:38:39.380 --> 00:38:40.520
we weren't random killers.

00:38:40.520 --> 00:38:42.050
We didn't do drive-by shootings.

00:38:42.050 --> 00:38:43.440
We weren't allowed to do that stuff.

00:38:43.440 --> 00:38:44.630
We didn't do it.

00:38:44.630 --> 00:38:47.570
Any murder in that life had
to be sanctioned by the boss.

00:38:47.570 --> 00:38:50.350
That was it, it had to be
sanctioned by the boss.

00:38:50.350 --> 00:38:51.740
There was discussion about it,

00:38:51.740 --> 00:38:54.480
some people were for it,
some people were against it,

00:38:54.480 --> 00:38:56.470
and then a ruling was made.

00:38:56.470 --> 00:39:01.070
And, you know, I always
thought about this,

00:39:01.070 --> 00:39:03.407
I said, "Look, this life was like a wheel,

00:39:03.407 --> 00:39:05.617
"it turns around, you know.

00:39:05.617 --> 00:39:09.437
"One day if I'm sitting there,
you know, giving a vote,

00:39:09.437 --> 00:39:12.897
"deciding the fate of
somebody, I wannabe hesitant.

00:39:12.897 --> 00:39:15.503
"I'm not gonna be the one to
say right away, 'Let's do this.

00:39:15.503 --> 00:39:16.336
"'or let's do that,

00:39:16.336 --> 00:39:18.367
"'or, you know, put a
death warrant on this guy,'

00:39:18.367 --> 00:39:20.947
"because it might be me
sitting there one day.

00:39:20.947 --> 00:39:24.037
"I mean, it might be me that
they're deciding upon one day,

00:39:24.037 --> 00:39:26.597
"and I wanna be known
to be the guy that said,

00:39:26.597 --> 00:39:27.837
"'Let's really discuss this.

00:39:27.837 --> 00:39:28.670
"'Let's wait.

00:39:28.670 --> 00:39:29.740
"'Let's see.'"

00:39:29.740 --> 00:39:32.910
And, you know, I think in
the end that's served me well

00:39:33.770 --> 00:39:35.620
because I had an experience
where I was brought

00:39:35.620 --> 00:39:36.580
into a room one night,

00:39:36.580 --> 00:39:38.920
I didn't know if I was gonna walk out,

00:39:38.920 --> 00:39:42.340
an experience that prepared
me for walking away later on

00:39:42.340 --> 00:39:44.880
because, honestly, I learned
through that experience

00:39:44.880 --> 00:39:46.647
that I could face death.

00:39:46.647 --> 00:39:47.603
- [Mark] "Cause they were suspicious

00:39:47.603 --> 00:39:49.792
that you were up to--
- Yeah.

00:39:49.792 --> 00:39:50.740
I mean, I was called into a room

00:39:50.740 --> 00:39:52.470
under some very bad circumstances.

00:39:52.470 --> 00:39:54.584
And the way the setup was--

00:39:54.584 --> 00:39:56.525
- [Mark] What was a story?

00:39:56.525 --> 00:39:59.360
You know, look making a lot
of money in the gas business,

00:39:59.360 --> 00:40:03.350
you know, and word was getting out,

00:40:03.350 --> 00:40:05.340
and, like I said, my boss was going after

00:40:05.340 --> 00:40:07.707
finding some people, seeing if
I was turning in enough money

00:40:07.707 --> 00:40:08.870
and all this kind of stuff.

00:40:08.870 --> 00:40:10.860
I'm turning in millions, you know.

00:40:10.860 --> 00:40:13.520
Story came out that I was making billions.

00:40:13.520 --> 00:40:15.137
My attitude would have
been, "Well, so what.

00:40:15.137 --> 00:40:15.970
"He's taken all the risks.

00:40:15.970 --> 00:40:16.803
"He's doing this.

00:40:16.803 --> 00:40:17.636
"He's making me wealthy.

00:40:17.636 --> 00:40:18.469
"What do I care?"

00:40:18.469 --> 00:40:20.450
But it's not like that with everybody.

00:40:20.450 --> 00:40:23.010
So, I think, you know, when I look at it

00:40:23.010 --> 00:40:24.510
they wanted to put a scare into me.

00:40:24.510 --> 00:40:28.820
Maybe, maybe it was serious
more than I thought afterwards.

00:40:28.820 --> 00:40:29.743
I don't know.

00:40:29.743 --> 00:40:30.750
- [Mark] But you know,

00:40:30.750 --> 00:40:32.520
from experience walking
into a room like that.

00:40:32.520 --> 00:40:33.353
- Oh, yeah.

00:40:33.353 --> 00:40:34.186
Let me tell you something.

00:40:34.186 --> 00:40:38.380
It was about a 30 yard walk
from the car that I get out of

00:40:38.380 --> 00:40:41.350
to the basement of an apartment, a room,

00:40:41.350 --> 00:40:42.360
it was a private house,

00:40:42.360 --> 00:40:45.230
but we had to go into the
basement down the steps.

00:40:45.230 --> 00:40:46.063
And it was late at night,

00:40:46.063 --> 00:40:47.210
it was a summer night,

00:40:47.210 --> 00:40:49.180
I can tell you this.

00:40:49.180 --> 00:40:52.197
The way it lined up, I said, "I'm dead.

00:40:52.197 --> 00:40:53.880
"I'm not walking out of here."

00:40:53.880 --> 00:40:57.330
When I walked down that path,
as I think about it now,

00:40:57.330 --> 00:40:59.490
I can hear the crickets chirping

00:40:59.490 --> 00:41:03.000
and I can almost smell the
night air, the flowers,

00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:06.523
my senses got so acute at that point.

00:41:07.942 --> 00:41:09.487
And, you know, I've said this
before and people said to me,

00:41:09.487 --> 00:41:11.410
"Why didn't you cut and run?"

00:41:11.410 --> 00:41:13.010
And I said, "I don't know."

00:41:13.010 --> 00:41:14.210
I mean, it was just robotic.

00:41:14.210 --> 00:41:16.400
I said, "Hey, if this is it, this is it."

00:41:16.400 --> 00:41:18.810
But I will tell you
this, you know, my heart

00:41:18.810 --> 00:41:20.210
was beating out of my chest,

00:41:20.210 --> 00:41:21.630
and when that door opened,

00:41:21.630 --> 00:41:23.700
I don't know how I didn't just cave in.

00:41:23.700 --> 00:41:25.410
'Cause I thought, you
know, I know the set-up,

00:41:25.410 --> 00:41:27.810
guy stand up, boom, you're
done, it's over with.

00:41:29.510 --> 00:41:32.330
But it taught me later on
that I could face death.

00:41:32.330 --> 00:41:33.770
So when I did walk away

00:41:33.770 --> 00:41:35.900
and I knew that I'd have that trouble,

00:41:35.900 --> 00:41:37.207
I said, "Hey, you know what?

00:41:37.207 --> 00:41:38.697
"They're not gonna walk me into a room.

00:41:38.697 --> 00:41:40.510
"They're gonna have to come and get me."

00:41:40.510 --> 00:41:43.510
And I knew what to do to
change my lifestyle around,

00:41:43.510 --> 00:41:45.450
so I didn't make it easy for anybody

00:41:46.510 --> 00:41:48.410
'cause there was, you
know, a couple of attempts,

00:41:48.410 --> 00:41:49.670
I mean, I know that for a fact.

00:41:49.670 --> 00:41:50.760
- [Mark] After you left?

00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:51.820
- Yeah, oh yeah.
- Oh, really?

00:41:51.820 --> 00:41:54.980
- There was a crew that
was sent out to California

00:41:54.980 --> 00:41:57.803
and the FBI intercepted it,

00:41:58.757 --> 00:42:00.157
and they actually came to
my house and they said,

00:42:00.157 --> 00:42:03.237
"If you don't leave, you're
gonna be dead by Sunday.

00:42:03.237 --> 00:42:04.070
"That's the deal."

00:42:04.070 --> 00:42:06.370
'Cause, fortunately, at
that time they had a lot

00:42:06.370 --> 00:42:07.793
of informants on the street.

00:42:09.349 --> 00:42:11.200
And my wife was a wreck,
they told her too,

00:42:11.200 --> 00:42:12.787
and I got mad at them and they said,

00:42:12.787 --> 00:42:15.720
"Well, we wanted to make
sure that you left."

00:42:15.720 --> 00:42:17.210
Whether they like it or not,

00:42:17.210 --> 00:42:18.380
if you have a death threat on you

00:42:18.380 --> 00:42:20.390
they're obligated to come and tell you.

00:42:20.390 --> 00:42:21.900
So we had to pick up and move and leave

00:42:21.900 --> 00:42:23.530
for a couple of days,

00:42:23.530 --> 00:42:24.543
until I knew it was over with.

00:42:24.543 --> 00:42:27.321
so I had a couple of calls like that.

00:42:27.321 --> 00:42:28.520
- [Mark] But when you
come back to your house,

00:42:28.520 --> 00:42:29.980
(chuckles) you're being
careful to walk the dog.

00:42:29.980 --> 00:42:31.610
- Well, yeah, well, you know

00:42:31.610 --> 00:42:33.157
you don't create patterns in your life.

00:42:33.157 --> 00:42:34.920
You don't walk your dog at the same time.

00:42:34.920 --> 00:42:36.290
You don't go to the same restaurant.

00:42:36.290 --> 00:42:37.890
You don't hang out in
places where you know

00:42:37.890 --> 00:42:40.240
other guys hang out, wanna be a hero.

00:42:40.240 --> 00:42:42.070
So, you know, I was very disciplined

00:42:42.070 --> 00:42:43.970
because I knew I had to be.

00:42:43.970 --> 00:42:46.997
But, you know, it was tough.

00:42:46.997 --> 00:42:49.193
And like I said, a lot
of treachery in that life

00:42:49.193 --> 00:42:51.235
that you've gotta watch.

00:42:51.235 --> 00:42:54.090
And, you know, look, I'm
as honest as I can be

00:42:54.090 --> 00:42:54.923
about the life.

00:42:54.923 --> 00:42:58.240
And I've told people this,
that life is an evil lifestyle

00:42:58.240 --> 00:43:00.810
just like the gang life,
you know, it's evil.

00:43:00.810 --> 00:43:02.320
Now, I'm not calling the guy's evil,

00:43:02.320 --> 00:43:03.160
I was one of them.

00:43:03.160 --> 00:43:05.180
I just happened to be a very
fortunate, very blessed,

00:43:05.180 --> 00:43:08.280
but the lifestyle is
evil because I don't know

00:43:08.280 --> 00:43:11.070
any family of any member of that life,

00:43:11.070 --> 00:43:14.300
and this includes gangbangers
that I went to prison with,

00:43:14.300 --> 00:43:16.040
that hasn't been totally devastated.

00:43:16.040 --> 00:43:18.020
I mean, devastated, including my own,

00:43:18.020 --> 00:43:19.620
and not my wife and kids,

00:43:19.620 --> 00:43:21.730
but my mother, father, brothers, sisters,

00:43:21.730 --> 00:43:23.080
the family's destroyed.

00:43:23.080 --> 00:43:26.030
I don't even know how I came
out of there with a, you know,

00:43:26.980 --> 00:43:28.563
at least somewhat sane.

00:43:29.810 --> 00:43:31.220
People questioned that but (chuckles).

00:43:31.220 --> 00:43:33.040
- [Mark] Your story's incredible.

00:43:33.040 --> 00:43:35.340
You survived and thrived.

00:43:35.340 --> 00:43:37.480
- So any lifestyle that
does that to families

00:43:37.480 --> 00:43:39.350
has to be evil, and
that's the bottom line.

00:43:39.350 --> 00:43:40.410
I mean, you've got to stay away from that.

00:43:40.410 --> 00:43:41.947
That's what I tell these gangbangers,

00:43:41.947 --> 00:43:44.050
"You guys are out of your mind."

00:43:44.050 --> 00:43:47.320
- [Mark] And were these kind
of thoughts in your head,

00:43:47.320 --> 00:43:49.220
what helped you kind of change your ways

00:43:49.220 --> 00:43:50.140
and decide to leave?

00:43:50.140 --> 00:43:53.370
Or were there other
factors in your life also?.

00:43:53.370 --> 00:43:55.880
- Leaving that life was one of the,

00:43:55.880 --> 00:43:59.330
if not the most difficult
decision I ever made,

00:43:59.330 --> 00:44:02.060
because look I took the
oath very seriously,

00:44:02.060 --> 00:44:04.213
I'm my father's son, I love my dad.

00:44:05.450 --> 00:44:08.240
I would go to sleep at
night, leaving the the life,

00:44:08.240 --> 00:44:10.330
wake up, going back in.

00:44:10.330 --> 00:44:11.950
I mean, I was so torn.

00:44:11.950 --> 00:44:16.020
It was so difficult emotionally for me

00:44:16.020 --> 00:44:17.670
'cause I didn't wanna be known as a guy

00:44:17.670 --> 00:44:19.890
that betrayed an oath,
whether it was right or wrong.

00:44:19.890 --> 00:44:22.580
'Cause look, I had a very
idealistic view of that life,

00:44:22.580 --> 00:44:24.430
when I came in, I was gung ho,

00:44:24.430 --> 00:44:26.930
I'm gonna be part of
something my father's part of,

00:44:26.930 --> 00:44:28.740
there's brotherhood among men.

00:44:28.740 --> 00:44:32.190
It was exhilarating, and I
took it extremely seriously.

00:44:32.190 --> 00:44:35.560
So leaving that life was
very, very difficult.

00:44:35.560 --> 00:44:36.393
It really was.

00:44:36.393 --> 00:44:39.810
I mean, sometimes, you
know, even at a moment,

00:44:39.810 --> 00:44:42.197
I mean, I feel it today,
every once in a while.

00:44:42.197 --> 00:44:45.290
- [Mark ] But the government's
becoming more effective

00:44:46.340 --> 00:44:48.070
played a part in all this as well.

00:44:48.070 --> 00:44:50.350
- You've gotta be out of your
mind to me to be in that life.

00:44:50.350 --> 00:44:51.930
You're going to jail or you going down,

00:44:51.930 --> 00:44:53.920
one way or the other at one point in time.

00:44:53.920 --> 00:44:55.270
Especially, it was too late for me,

00:44:55.270 --> 00:44:57.020
I became too high profile.

00:44:57.020 --> 00:44:58.650
Once you got that bullseye on your back

00:44:58.650 --> 00:45:00.530
you've got that target,
they'll never let you go.

00:45:00.530 --> 00:45:03.160
They've got all the time, all
the money, all the resources,

00:45:03.160 --> 00:45:03.993
so they're gonna get you.

00:45:03.993 --> 00:45:06.853
And when they do get you,
it's over, that's it.

00:45:09.700 --> 00:45:12.870
- [Mark] What do you enjoy
most about your life now,

00:45:12.870 --> 00:45:15.570
that's treasury free? (laughs)

00:45:15.570 --> 00:45:16.470
Your new life is what?

00:45:16.470 --> 00:45:19.081
You have a wife, you have kids, you have--

00:45:19.081 --> 00:45:20.870
- I've got a, you know,
a wife that I'm very

00:45:20.870 --> 00:45:22.093
much in love with 34 years.
- You live in California.

00:45:22.093 --> 00:45:24.170
- Yeah we live out in Southern Cal.

00:45:24.170 --> 00:45:25.264
I've got seven great kids, you know,

00:45:25.264 --> 00:45:27.010
three from my first marriage,

00:45:27.010 --> 00:45:29.820
but they all love each
other, which is great.

00:45:29.820 --> 00:45:31.640
Look, I live a good lifestyle.

00:45:31.640 --> 00:45:33.760
I mean, you know, I'm
speaking all over the world

00:45:33.760 --> 00:45:36.710
having a positive impact on people,

00:45:36.710 --> 00:45:39.020
being a source of encouragement and hope,

00:45:39.020 --> 00:45:40.920
which is extremely gratifying.

00:45:40.920 --> 00:45:43.730
I really learned in my
life, it really is better

00:45:43.730 --> 00:45:44.770
to give than receive.

00:45:44.770 --> 00:45:47.299
You get a better feeling
out of it, you know,

00:45:47.299 --> 00:45:48.132
and what else can you give me,

00:45:48.132 --> 00:45:50.570
I've gotten everything
just about in my life.

00:45:50.570 --> 00:45:52.310
It motivates me, keeps me going.

00:45:52.310 --> 00:45:53.280
I'm very fortunate.

00:45:53.280 --> 00:45:54.960
I am a person of faith.

00:45:54.960 --> 00:45:57.800
Look, my faith has played a major role

00:45:57.800 --> 00:45:59.570
because without God in my life

00:45:59.570 --> 00:46:00.890
I don't think I'd be sitting here now.

00:46:00.890 --> 00:46:02.250
I mean, I know that for a fact,

00:46:02.250 --> 00:46:05.930
so, you know, and things
I've had my challenges

00:46:05.930 --> 00:46:08.510
and my struggles, don't get me wrong.

00:46:08.510 --> 00:46:11.000
I didn't get a lobotomy when
I became a person of faith,

00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:13.180
I still have tendencies
where I could jump back

00:46:13.180 --> 00:46:15.673
in mob life for a
second, but I try not to.

00:46:16.531 --> 00:46:17.364
And I've got the right people around me

00:46:17.364 --> 00:46:18.340
keeping me accountable.

00:46:18.340 --> 00:46:21.333
So, you know, it's all working out.

00:46:22.540 --> 00:46:25.178
- [Mark] Excellent, what
a great, great story.

00:46:25.178 --> 00:46:26.011
- Thank you.

00:46:26.011 --> 00:46:27.530
- Michael, thank you
very much for sharing it.

00:46:27.530 --> 00:46:28.700
- Appreciate it, thank you.

00:46:28.700 --> 00:46:29.650
- [Mark] Thank you.

